 {:seon.task/name "main-runs-spawn-on-one-fixed-branch"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-11-12 (Tests, turning prove-main-on-commit on): a run of main spawns its prove agent on the one branch :tests (seon.prove/request's {:op :spawn :opts {:branch :tests}}). A run that supersedes main's earlier run spawns while the earlier agent is still ending (runner-done's kill is asked, not awaited), so the spawn is refused (:seon.system/refused, branch held by a live agent) and the run answers that error and a platform problem; the next program commit runs again. Never a hang, but a lost run. Correct: the superseding run spawns once the earlier runner's end is recorded (@(c/kill! ...) answers then, jolt/killend), or each run's agent takes a branch of its own key, dropped with it. Proof, red first: two main commits in a burst give one run of the latest, answered green, and no refused spawn."
